+# Reference-led garage composition
+
+Owner reference, 2026-10-12. GC22: room composition and layout; GC23: stylish right trophy alcove, workshop back wall and left poster; GC24: material/light/image clarity. Preserve GC06–GC21/CW13/CW15/CW16/V06/G01/R01/Q01. The supplied image is an art/layout target, not a shipping asset or evidence of this implementation achieving its quality level.
+
+Garage now has a centred wider room view, lower viewing elevation and a left-facing three-quarter vehicle pose on the retained turntable. The main camera uses 40° FOV, atan(0.16) elevation, a 1.48 presentation-distance multiplier and a 0.45m higher view target. This gives the room and its ceiling structure space around the car. Explicit Reset restores the revised framing; switching cars still retains the actual camera/zoom/tilt/yaw. Thumbnail cameras keep their closer framing. All five actual 3D cards fit at 1600px and the supplied reference's approximately 1720px width; smaller windows keep swiping and complete cards. Bottom Select car, the left rail and the general backdrop remain. Header shading is lighter and shallower to reveal the architecture while keeping text legible.
+
+The right side wall holds one uninterrupted open display alcove rather than six divided cubbies: deep returns, brushed gold trim, visible perimeter light strips, three warm spotlights, six future-award bases and handleless lower storage. An original laurel/Beat my track mural is permanent decor, not an earned trophy. The existing separate trophy camera now faces this wider display, easing in and returning to the car on submenu selection. No award ownership or grants are fabricated; the wall remains empty until future award integration.
+
+All functional garage equipment is on the back wall: shutter and runners, a workbench/pegboard with ring/open-ended tools and screwdrivers, complete spare wheels, a red drawer cabinet, supply shelves, bottles, toolboxes, formed safety cans and a compressor. Rear wall lamps produce warm pools; roof trusses have triangular webs and suspended luminaires. The left wall has an original framed typographic poster, with restrained gold diagonal artwork. A plant and floor trim support the display corner. The room uses original batched bevelled geometry and the existing full/thumbnail PackedScene caches; it adds no imported/generated reference media, external dependency, vendor or runtime AI.
+
+Concrete has interpolated mottling, fine grain, panel seams, controlled roughness/metallic response, warm display light wash and soft analytic reflections of the two authored roof luminaires. These reflections are a limited shader approximation of those lights, not reflected room/car geometry, SSR or ray tracing. Static furnishing contact shadows give the equipment grounding. Garage surfaces use smooth diffuse lighting while existing vehicle paint/glass/weathering remain separate.
+
+The showroom previously rendered at logical UI dimensions and was then enlarged with the window. Main and card viewports now render through their own TextureRect at the displayed pixel density, with 4x/2x MSAA respectively, full 3D buffer scale and an aspect-preserving 2560x1440 limit. Actual logged main sizes: 876x279 at 960x540; 1168x372 at 1280x720; 1488x372 at 1600x720; 1578x472 at 1720x914, replacing a 1242x372 render at that last size. A 960px window avoids needless oversampling. Thumbnails remain demonstrably frozen between explicit refreshes. Input/picking still converts logical controls to actual viewport pixels. This is menu presentation only; the driving render scale/camera and canonical model/handling/scoring remain unchanged.
+
+Changed runtime: `game/ui/garage_environment.gd`, `garage_details.gd`, `garage_floor.gdshader`, `car_showroom.gd`, `garage_page.gd`. Added `game/ui/garage_workshop.gd` (+UID), `game/tests/capture_garage_reference.gd` (+UID). Documentation: this file, `AGENTS.md`, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`, `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`.
+
+Actual commands on pinned `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`, isolated test records:
+
+```powershell
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action Import
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_garage_reference.gd -Graphical
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_garage_reference.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod mobile -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/garage-reference-2026-10-12/mobile/clean'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_carousel.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--capture-gallery-motion=res://../docs/evidence/garage-reference-2026-10-12'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_carousel.gd -Graphical -RenderingMethod mobile -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/garage-reference-2026-10-12/mobile'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_car_transition.gd -Graphical -TestArgument '--evidence-root=res://../docs/evidence/garage-reference-2026-10-12/transition'
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_view_controls.gd -Graphical
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_car_wash.gd -Graphical
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_studio.gd -Graphical
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd -Graphical
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action Doctor
+python build/encode_garage_reference_motion.py
+python build/checkpoint_garage_reference.py
+```
+
+Final passes: reference layout **25 Compatibility + 25 desktop Mobile/Vulkan**; carousel/navigation/local cosmetics/frozen 3D cards/fixed-room turntable/trophy camera **295 Compatibility including 120 actual motion frames + 175 Mobile**; retained-zoom/car-transition **23**, view controls **59**, manual washing/local condition **1,402**, exact native model/glazing/render regression **80**, all zero failures. Import passes. Shared menu gestures **268 checks**, zero failures. Native Compact remains 64 meshes/104,558 triangles/68,996 UV vertices, with baked/source car and glazing byte equality. Final isolated RTX 3090 Compatibility sample: 407.677ms cold page creation; viewport CPU median/p95 0.811/1.059ms, GPU median/p95 0.189/2.256ms. These are desktop diagnostic samples, not a speedup claim, a complete application benchmark or phone proof.
+
+Inspected [reference-size garage](evidence/garage-reference-2026-10-12/clean/garage-1720.png), [1280](evidence/garage-reference-2026-10-12/clean/garage-1280.png), [trophy alcove](evidence/garage-reference-2026-10-12/clean/trophy-wall.png), all-five-car clean views and matching Mobile captures. Clean fixture saves are isolated and create no condition records. Ordinary condition tests still deliberately show accumulated dirt. Initial framing cropped the poster/roof and concealed the trim lights; camera/placement and light-strip depth were corrected after render inspection. Leaf planes were made double-sided, and blocky concrete noise was replaced with interpolation. No original invariant assertion was removed or weakened.
+
+Actual [trophy camera movement](evidence/garage-reference-2026-10-12/trophy-camera-motion.png) is a lossless 120-frame 960x540 APNG, assembled directly from Godot renders using Python stdlib with CRC/format checks. Four-second 30fps playback is for review, not performance measurement. The animation is approximately 34MB; raw frames are in `build/garage-trophy-motion-2026-10-12`. Baseline sources, captures, logs, scoped patch and hash ledger: `docs/evidence/garage-reference-2026-10-12`; isolated two-commit checkpoint: `build/garage_reference/checkpoint-repo`. Main branch/index and concurrent unrelated work are preserved. Viewport behavior was checked against the official [Viewport](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_viewport.html) and [SubViewportContainer](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_subviewportcontainer.html) documentation and the actual pinned-engine runs above.
+
+Doctor found no attached Android device. No phone input/thermal/performance test, APK export/install, full Validate, physics merge/regression, backend operation or deployment was performed. Owner reference/style/material acceptance remains: this is an implemented layout and presentation revision, not a claim of matching every detail or the reference's AAA quality. Physical-device frame pacing/memory, brightness, poster readability, sustained orbit/zoom/wash and future award storage/models/population remain open.
